# L §8.4 R-load (tally 2.1.7 R5, #144; the review's finding 3, pick P41): load makes every check whose inputs it sees
# "on every item, whatever the asks read": a value(broker, d) in PLN with no by, in a def no ask reads, over a place
# of unit any that buy's leg writes EUR into, is LOAD-PRICE at load, at its line. refcore 2.1.7 loaded it clean and
# answered k (the twin of L5_10_load_price_run, whose ask reads the value).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind brokerages: place any min 0
kind fx_buys: event certain
  leg eur: EUR
  leg cash: PLN

input buy_day: date
input vd: date
input eur_amt: money EUR
input pln_amt: money PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move buy: fx_buys
  on buy_day
  leg eur from market to broker amount eur_amt
  leg cash from konto to market amount pln_amt

def unread: num PLN = value(broker, vd) in PLN

ask k: bal(konto, buy_day)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  brokerages + [broker] lives 2026-01-01..
  buy_day = 2026-03-02
  vd = 2026-06-30
  eur_amt = 100.00 EUR
  pln_amt = 425.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PRICE value(broker) in PLN holds units in EUR and states no by (m.tally:29)
